All claims require a diagnosis code and an CPT code. I’ve seen cases of insurance fraud while reviewing orders sent from doctors. 

All of them were fraudulent in a way that would make the patient denied when they should have been approved.

The AMA CPT Advisor Editorial Panel is meeting on Feb 3, 2025 to release official guidance for Prior Authorization CPT code billing. 

The guidance will detail what doctors can get paid for + what is a free service to health insurance companies. 

